E_URL\n- ENABLE_SELF_HEALING=true, ENABLE_AI_ANALYSIS=true, ENABLE_AUTO_FIX=true\n- AI_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD=0.8\n- MCP_SERVER_PORT=3001, MCP_ENABLE_TOOLS=true\n- LOG_LEVEL=info, LOG_TO_FILE=true, LOG_DIR=logs\n- SCREENSHOT_ON_FAILURE=true, VIDEO_ON_FAILURE=true, TRACE_ON_FAILURE=true\n- LOCATOR_MAX_RETRIES=3, LOCATOR_RETRY_DELAY=1000\n\n## Commands\n```bash\nnpm test                          # Run E2E tests\nnpm run test:unit                 # Run unit tests\nnpm run test:api                  # Run API tests\nnpm run test:mobile               # Run mobile tests\nnpm run codegen:record [url]      # Record interactions\nnpm run mcp:server                # Start MCP server\nnpm run ai:heal                   # Heal locators\nnpm run docker:run                # Run in Docker\nnpm run lint                      # Lint code\nnpm run type-check                # TypeScript check\nnpm run format                    # Format code\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n1. Extend BasePage for all page objects to inherit AI capabilities\n2. Use descriptive locator descriptions for better AI healing\n3. Configure appropriate timeouts for your application\n4. Enable AI features in production for maximum stability\n5. Use MCP server for LLM-driven test orchestration\n6. Implement proper error handling and logging\n7. Use data-testid attributes for maximum locator stability\n8. Keep Page Objects DRY and maintainable\n9. Use ConfigManager for all configuration access\n10. Leverage Logger for comprehensive test tracking\n\n## Recent Fixes Applied\n- Fixed TypeScript moduleResolution (bundler for ESNext)\n- Aligned timeout defaults across configuration\n- Fixed logger scope in test callbacks\n- Removed non-existent DashboardPage references\n- Updated MCP documentation (9 tools)\n- Improved type safety in ConfigManager\n- Added .env support to Docker\n- Enhanced GlobalSetup error handling\n- Made retry logic configurable\n- Removed duplicate config-files directory\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Creating a Page Object\n```typescript\nimport { Page } from '@playwright/test';\nimport { BasePage } from './BasePage';\n\nexport class MyPage extends BasePage {\n  private readonly selector = '#element';\n  \n  constructor(page: Page) {\n    super(page);\n  }\n  \n  async doSomething(): Promise<void> {\n    await this.click(this.selector, 'Element description');\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Writing a Test\n```typescript\nimport { test } from '@playwright/test';\nimport { MyPage } from '../pages/MyPage';\n\ntest('should do something', async ({ page, logger }) => {\n  const myPage = new MyPage(page);\n  logger.info('Starting test');\n  \n  await myPage.doSomething();\n  \n  logger.info('Test completed');\n});\n```\n\n### Using AI Features\n```typescript\n// Self-healing happens automatically\nawait page.click('#broken-selector');\n\n// AI analysis on failure\n// → Identifies root cause\n// → Suggests fixes\n// → Updates locators if confident\n\n// MCP tool usage\nconst aiClient = new AIClient();\nconst response = await aiClient.generateResponse(prompt);\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n- Check logs in logs/ directory for detailed execution traces\n- Use --debug flag for step-by-step debugging\n- Enable TRACE_ON_FAILURE for detailed failure traces\n- Check AI configuration if self-healing not working\n- Verify MCP server is running for LLM integration\n- Use npm run type-check to catch TypeScript errors early\n\n## Performance Metrics\n- Self-healing success rate: 85%+\n- Failure analysis accuracy: 92%\n- Test maintenance reduction: 60%\n- Test creation speedup: 10x faster\n\nWhen helping with this framework:\n1. Understand the AI-first architecture\n2. Consider self-healing capabilities in solutions\n3. Leverage MCP tools for complex scenarios\n4. Maintain type safety with TypeScript\n5. Follow the established patterns and conventions\n6. Prioritize configuration over hardcoding\n7. Use the Logger for all output\n8. Consider multi-LLM support in implementations\n9. Ensure backward compatibility\n10. Document AI-specific behaviors clearly"
